# Generated geometry is reproducible from the schema -- regenerate with
# station/generate_hull.py rather than committing multi-megabyte meshes.
station/generated/*.obj
station/generated/*.glb
station/generated/*.glb
station/generated/hull_lod*.obj
godot/station.glb
godot/.godot/
renders/
station/generated/corridor.obj
station/__pycache__/
station/generated/interior_*.obj
station/generated/starfury.obj
godot/scripts/*.uid

# Per-shot scene assembly (tools/export_scene.py). Same argument as above --
# 44 MB of .glb regenerated from the schema on demand. Needs its own line
# because a gitignore "*" does not cross a directory separator, so the
# station/generated/*.glb rule above does not reach this subdirectory.
station/generated/scene/
tools/__pycache__/

# Python bytecode. Regenerated on every import; 14 of these were tracked.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Agent worktrees. `Agent(isolation: "worktree")` checks the repository out
# under here so a background agent can render and edit without racing the main
# tree -- 54 MB a copy, transient, and removed when the agent finishes. It is
# infrastructure, not content, and committing it would put a second copy of the
# whole project inside the project.
.claude/worktrees/

# station/variety.py's rebuilt-room cache. 8.6 MB of derived geometry keyed on
# the generators' own content hash -- `--rebuild` ignores it and `--verify-cache`
# diffs sampled rooms against it, so it is reproducible rather than authoritative.
# A cache that can go stale is a second copy of a computed number; this one is
# keyed so it cannot, and it does not belong in the repository either way.
.variety-cache/

# The economy ledger (`station/economy.py`). SESSION STATE, not content: stock
# levels, tills, wages and purses, written by `dockwork.py --loop` and read by
# `hud.gd`. Committing it would freeze one playthrough's world into the repo,
# and `Ledger.fresh()` rebuilds the opening balances from the register.
station/generated/economy.json

# C&C's persisted watch state, on the same grounds as `economy.json` above: it
# is world state a run WRITES, not content the repo owns, and committing it
# would freeze one watch's orders into the build. Added while the C&C agent was
# still running -- if it turns out this directory holds authored content rather
# than generated state, this line is the thing to delete.
station/generated/cnc/
scratchpad/till-run/head/
scratchpad/till-lurker/head/

# The commit mirror's own live log. `scratchpad/push_mirror.sh` appends a line
# every time it pushes, so committing it would be a file that changes every two
# minutes for as long as the guard is running. The SCRIPT is tracked; its
# runtime output is not.
scratchpad/push_mirror.log

# tools/package.sh output: a 324 MB staged build and a 113 MB tarball.
# Derived, like station/generated/, and for the same reason.
dist/
